# What Vercel does not need in order to build and serve qubix.university.
#
# Without this file every tracked file goes up on every deploy. That was 64.8 MB
# against a 1.3 MB site, almost all of it current-app/, which the build never
# reads: nothing in vite.config.js, src/ or scripts/ references it. Uploading it
# is pure waste, it makes every deploy slow, and on a poor connection it is the
# difference between a deploy landing and timing out.
#
# Nothing here is deleted or untracked. It stays in Git, where it belongs, and
# simply stops being sent to a host that has no use for it.

# The consolidated application and creative work. Canonical in Git, not served.
current-app/

# Native shells. Built by Capacitor from dist/, never by Vercel.
android/
ios/

# Authoring and governance material. The Factory is dev-only and the curriculum
# records are not part of the site.
supabase/

# Same shape as docs/: the curriculum records are not served, but
# release guards read the approval registers during prebuild.
curriculum/*
!curriculum/APPROVED-FIGURES.json
!curriculum/APPROVED-DSA.json

# docs/ is not served, but check-motion reads docs/MEDIA-RULE.md during
# prebuild and the deploy failed on ENOENT without it. The contents are
# excluded rather than the directory, because gitignore semantics cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is already excluded.
docs/*
!docs/MEDIA-RULE.md

# Local only.
.playwright-session/
*.log

# book/dist is the self-contained build, kept for sending as single files.
# What the site serves is public/library, produced from it by
# scripts/publish-library.mjs during prebuild. Shipping both would double
# roughly 7 MB for no reason.
book/dist/

# The generated quarter and its release archive. Both are large, both are
# gitignored, and a .vercelignore replaces .gitignore rather than adding to it,
# so without these lines 442 MB of local-only data went up on every deploy and
# the first attempt was rejected: sale_line.csv alone is 187 MB against a
# 100 MB per-file limit.
#
# Nothing in the build reads them. public/data/qubix-sample.db is rebuilt from
# the committed data-sample/ by scripts/build-sample-db.mjs during prebuild,
# which is also what the four figure guards read.
# Anchored to the root. Unanchored, `data/` matches a directory of that name at
# any depth, which quietly excluded src/lib/data/ and failed the Vercel build
# on "Could not resolve ../lib/data/superstore.js".
/data/
/dist-data/
